      "title": "Office Hours After the PASS Summit",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hjMdBoutVLg",
      "published_at": "2026-11-17T15:30:16+00:00",
      "author": "Brent Ozar Unlimited",
      "summary": "I'm back from the annual PASS Data Community Summit, so let's talk industry news before we dive into your 3 top-voted questions from https://pollgab.com/room/brento.\n\n00:00 Start\n00:05 News: the vibe at the PASS Summit in Seattle this week\n03:27 News: Microsoft's open Q&A about competing with PostgreSQL\n07:13 News: Microsoft demoing GPU usage in SQL Server query plans\n09:04 News: Patch Tuesday and bugs in SQL Server\n11:29 News: Microsoft Purview deprecated\n13:11 DBA_ReflectingHisCareerChoice: Microsoft retired Database Watchers. If your company used only Azure SQL DBs (incl. elastic pools), what would be your go-to monitoring tool? The open-source tools I know seem focused on on-prem SQL Server, not Azure SQL DB.\n14:51 MyTeaGotCold: How frequently do you need to go beyond what is shown in an actual execution plan? The only such methods I know of are sys.dm_exec_session_wait_stats, Windows Performance Recorder, and Trace Flag 2363. I don't recall seeing them in Mastering Query Tuning but it has been a while.\n16:03 DataBarbieAdministrator: In your opinion, why is the Failover Cluster Instance feature so rarely used in SQL Server? What do you think about that technology?",
